    "body": "Yeah I just stumbled across this one when reading the `figure` section closely today for other reasons. So I haven’t gone through the spec systematically at all to try to find other cases like this, but I reckon there are some others. The problem with not setting text off typographically in some way for this kind of a case is that it leads to ambiguity and confusion. So, just as we go out of our way to avoid ambiguity in the technical wording of algorithms, etc., in the spec, this is just a way of eliminating another general form of ambiguity.",
